imud-prometheus (1.10.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The bridges say when a heading is not referenced to north, each in its
    protocol's own terms rather than by all withholding it.  imud-signalk
    drops navigation.headingMagnetic/True/magneticVariation; imud-mqtt
    drops the matching topics, which are retained, and adds
    navigation/headingReferenced. imud-influxdb keeps publishing heading
    with heading_ref and mag_absent fields, and imud-prometheus keeps its
    gauge and adds imud_mag_uncal and imud_mag_absent. imud-mavlink gains
    SYS_STATUS, whose 3D_MAG present and health bits separate a board with
    no magnetometer from one that has stopped answering.
  * The armhf packages are now built on Raspbian at the ARMv6 baseline, so
    they run on every Raspberry Pi that boots a 32-bit userland.
    Previously they were built to Debian's ARMv7 baseline.  On a Pi 1 or
    Pi Zero/Zero W the previous packages installed without complaint and
    then died on an illegal instruction, because both ports report the
    same "armhf" architecture. Those boards can now install from the apt
    repository. The arm64 packages are unchanged.

 -- Richard Simpson <richcreations@gmail.com>  Sat, 05 Sep 2026 09:31:46 -0700

imud-prometheus (1.8.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New gauge imud_state_reset: the daemon's MEKF found a non-finite
    value in its own state and reset itself. It is latched until the
    filter re-converges rather than being a single-packet pulse, so it
    survives a scrape interval; imud_fusion_converged is 0 for the same
    span. Alert on it — the daemon is publishing attitude that has not
    settled, and the cause is usually a bad calibration file.
  * BEHAVIOUR CHANGE: a bad value in imud-prometheus.conf is now fatal,
    where it was previously accepted with no message at any log level.
    A value too long for its field — the bind address or the stream
    socket path — was truncated and used, so the bridge listened
    somewhere the operator never wrote. An out-of-range integer wrapped,
    so a listen_port of 4294977414 became port 10118. And nan, inf and
    1e999 loaded cleanly into any float key. listen_port is also now
    bounded to 1..65535, because 70000 fits an int perfectly well and
    then becomes port 4464 the moment htons() truncates it.
  * The daemon no longer leaves the binary stream socket bound with
    nothing behind it, so a bridge that connects is either served or
    refused. Previously a daemon whose stream thread failed to start
    still had the socket bound: the bridge connected successfully, into
    the backlog, and then waited forever — serving imud_up 1 with no
    gauges behind it, since it had connected. See the imud changelog.
  * No wire-format change: the packet stays v17 / 276 bytes.

 -- Richard Simpson <richcreations@gmail.com>  Wed, 05 Aug 2026 12:00:00 -0700

imud-prometheus (1.8.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: a scraper that connected and then sent nothing stalled the
    bridge. serve_scrape() did a blocking recv() under a 2 s receive
    timeout before building the page, so one silent connection froze the
    single-threaded loop — imud_read() included — for a full 2 s per
    iteration. Measured against a 50 Hz stream while holding one silent
    connection open across a 2.6 s window: 47 packets consumed before,
    112 after. The request is now read incrementally inside the loop's
    own poll, the accepted fd is non-blocking, and a client that goes
    quiet is dropped at its deadline. One scrape is still served at a
    time; the man page and spec claimed a slow scraper could not wedge
    the reader and now describe the actual mechanism.
  * BEHAVIOUR CHANGE: the bridge now runs with imud as its primary group
    and no longer belongs to gpio. It carried Group=gpio only to reach
    the stream socket — it touches no hardware — and the socket is now
    imud:imud. The bridge connects as the socket's owner either way, so
    this needs no coordinated upgrade.
  * Fix: a config file that exists but cannot be read is now fatal. It
    previously fell through to defaults, and since enabled defaults to
    false the bridge exited reporting "disabled in config
    ([imud-prometheus] enabled = false)" — naming the wrong cause
    entirely for what is a permissions problem.
  * Harden: tier-2 systemd sandboxing (empty CapabilityBoundingSet, a
    @system-service syscall allow-list, RestrictNamespaces,
    LockPersonality, RestrictSUIDSGID, ProtectHostname, ProtectClock,
    ProtectProc=invisible, ProcSubset=pid, UMask=0077), and every fd is
    close-on-exec — including the accepted scrape connection, which
    POSIX does not carry FD_CLOEXEC across.
  * Requires wire format v17 (packet 276 bytes), unchanged since 1.7.
    The gauge set, config keys and CLI are unchanged.

 -- Richard Simpson <richcreations@gmail.com>  Mon, 03 Aug 2026 12:00:00 -0700

imud-prometheus (1.7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Four new gauges from wire v17: imud_innov_weight_ratio and
    imud_innov_reject_ratio (MEKF update-gate health) and
    imud_nis_accel_ratio and imud_nis_mag_ratio (measurement-model
    consistency; 1 = the filter's covariance matches the innovations it
    sees, higher means over-confident).
  * Requires wire format v17 (packet 260 -> 276 bytes); must be upgraded
    together with the daemon.

